the Iowa caucuses typically force  candidates to lay out their farm program  platforms both president Trump and his  Democratic challenges are promising to  continue or expand programs that provide  large subsidies to farmers the one clear  difference between the president and  most of his challenges is that many  Democrats would direct more subsidies to  smaller farms the president also gave  farmers twenty five billion dollars in  ad-hoc market facilitation payments to  compensate them for the damages trade  policies have done to their revenues not  that there's much difference between mr.  Trump and most of the challenges on  trade like the president they seem to  believe that US exports are good the US  imports are bad so trade deals that  lower tariffs are bad only Michael  Bloomberg supports free trade finally  most candidates are paying little  attention to public funding for  agricultural research one program that  benefits farmers and consumers and keeps  us agriculture globally competitive  instead they prefer to spend taxpayer  dollars on direct deposit subsidies to  farmers to win their rural votes what do  you think about the presidential  candidates farm programs let us know in  our poll also let us know what other  topics you'd like our scholars to cover  in 60 seconds and be sure to LIKE and  subscribe for more research and videos  from AEI
 

